record.content:
The following is a contributed topic on known quantum paradoxes
(but no `quasi-paradoxes', please!)

\section{Quantum Paradoxes and Bell's inequalities}

There are two major known quantum `paradoxes':

\begin{enumerate}
\item 1. The Scr\"odinger's cat paradox,
often expressed as the ``Scr\"odinger's cat is neither dead nor alive'',
but in fact meaning something quite different;

\item 2. The EPR `Paradox'


\end{enumerate}
